and we begin this morning with the  investigation of Special Counsel Robert  Muller on election tampering which has  led to the first indictments of Russian  nationals more than a dozen are charged  with conspiracy to tamper with the  election process in an effort to  undermine confidence in US democracy  there is no allegation in the indictment  that anyone in the Trump campaign was  knowingly involved president Trump was  briefed on the matter Friday afternoon  the president ignored shouted questions  from reporters before he left Washington  for a weekend at his Mar Lago Resort  Errol Barnett is with the president in  West Palm Beach  Erol good morning good morning the  Russia investigation was bolstered by  the Deputy Attorney General announcing  in detail charges against Russian  nationals and Russian companies which in  and of itself is unprecedented but with  national security under threat president  Trump chose to comment on his personal  vindication the defendants allegedly  conducted what they called information  warfare against the United States Deputy  Attorney General Rod Rosenstein said  Russian nationals using stolen  identities posing as politically active  Americans had a clear and consistent  goal the Russian conspirators want to  promote discord in the United States and  undermine public confidence in democracy  prosecutors say the operation began in  2014 and was run out of this building in  st. Petersburg Russia according to the  37 page indictment 13 Russian nationals  and three Russian companies with a  budget of more than 1.2 million dollars  per month made hundreds of fake social  media profiles posting attacks on  Hillary Clinton while applauding Bernie  Sanders and then Canada Donald Trump  Rosenstein and FBI director Christopher  ray previously briefed President Trump  on this indictment in a statement the  White House said there was no collusion  between the Trump campaign and Russia  noting the outcome of the election was  not changed or affected  court documents show Russian operatives  were told to quote use any opportunity  to criticize Hillary Clinton and the  except Sanders and Trump we support them  that was a Democrat hoax it was an  excuse for losing the election president  Trump repeatedly calls the special  counsels probe a hoax tweeting yesterday  the Trump campaign did nothing wrong no  collusion investigators believe the  Russian agenda was also aimed to  suppress minority turnout an Instagram  message from a fake group called woke  blacks discouraged voting for either  party's nominee we could not resort to  the lesser of two Devils it said then  we'd surely be better off without voting  at all but Rosenstein emphasized this  indictment does not claim any American  knowingly played a role in the operation  the nature of the scheme was that the  defendants took extraordinary steps to  make it appear that they were ordinary  American political activists our  Republican House Speaker Paul Ryan says  Washington needs to follow the facts in  the wake of these charges while  Democratic leaders like Senator Chuck  Schumer say this is more proof President  Trump needs to implement the sanctions  against Russia approved by Congress  Anthony  Errol Barnett with the president in  Florida thanks Errol
 

